{"name":"Glitchy Shader Blue","hex":"#99ffff","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"glitchy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Prone to glitches.","Characteristic of glitch or error."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glitchy"},{"term":"shader","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One who, or that which, shades.","A set of software instructions used to calculate rendering effects on graphics hardware."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shader"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Glitch","blocks":[{"text":"A glitch is a brief technical fault, such as a transient one that corrects itself, making it difficult to troubleshoot. The term is particularly common in the computing and electronics industries, in circuit bending, as well as among players of video games, although any purposely organized structure, such as speech, may experience glitches."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Glitch_Train_Station_Display.jpg/330px-Glitch_Train_Station_Display.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glitch","wikidata":"Q543281"},{"title":"Shader","blocks":[{"text":"In computer graphics, a shader is a programmable operation which is applied to data as it moves through the rendering pipeline. Shaders act on data such as vertices and primitives, generate or morph geometries and fragments, and calculate the colors in a rendered image."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/Activemarker2.PNG/330px-Activemarker2.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shader","wikidata":"Q633182"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Virtual_Boy_glitch_in_right_eyepiece.jpg/500px-Virtual_Boy_glitch_in_right_eyepiece.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Virtual_Boy_glitch_in_right_eyepiece.jpg/1280px-Virtual_Boy_glitch_in_right_eyepiece.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Virtual_Boy_glitch_in_right_eyepiece.jpg/500px-Virtual_Boy_glitch_in_right_eyepiece.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The start-up screen of the Virtual Boy is affected by a visual glitch.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVirtual_Boy_glitch_in_right_eyepiece.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wik